      <h2>8. Impact on Pensions and the Unified Pension Scheme (UPS)</h2>
      <p>
        The fitment factor directly determines retirement benefits:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pension Parity for Past Retirees:</strong> In accordance with the Modified Parity Principle, existing civil and defence pensions are recalculated by applying the finalized fitment multiplier directly to basic pension, resetting Dearness Relief (DR) to 0%.</li>
        <li><strong>Integration with the Unified Pension Scheme (UPS):</strong> Because the UPS guarantees an assured pension of 50% of the average basic pay drawn in the final 12 months of qualifying service, a higher fitment factor permanently elevates the baseline for assured retirement pensions.</li>
      </ul>

